 "topics": [
  {
   "topic": "load_installation handling and reporting of over-depth configurations",
   "members": [
    "r2.00",
    "r3.00"
   ],
   "runs": [
    2,
    3
   ],
   "questions": [
    "Must `installation.load_installation` reject an over-depth configuration before parsing it, where exactly does that check occur in its ordered checks, and what failing check must its refusal name?",
    "When an otherwise-valid configuration exceeds json_depth_max, which ordered load_installation check and reason must be reported?"
   ],
   "units": [
    "context"
   ],
   "id": "T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "answered_later",
    "quotes": [
     "read_configuration: [VALIDATION_ERROR] MUST raise InstallationRejectedError naming the first failing check, in this order: config_path is not an absolute path; it cannot be opened component by component without following a symbolic link at any component, each component with os.O_NOFOLLOW, whose presence is never tested, each directory on the way also with os.O_PATH and os.O_DIRECTORY and the file itself also with os.O_NONBLOCK (A17), the file so opened is not a regular file, is not owned by the process's effective user, or grants any permission to group or others; the bytes cannot be read, have a json_depth above the imported RELEASE_CEILING_JSON_DEPTH_MAX constant, measured on the bytes before they are parsed, or do not parse as one JSON object whose members are exactly the fields of Installation with their types; a service appears twice in service_instances or in service_credentials; a credential header name is not an HTTP field-name token (one or more of the token characters of RFC 9110: letters, digits and the symbols allowed there); a credential's secret_file is not an absolute path; the owner token or any agent token is shorter than the imported ACCESS_TOKEN_LENGTH_MIN constant; two tokens among the owner token and the agent tokens are equal; two agent tokens have the same name. The ownership, mode and regular-file checks and the read MUST all use that one opened file, so the file checked is the file read.",
     "load_installation: [BEHAVIOR] MUST call read_configuration once at start, keep the returned Installation for the life of the process, and keep the SHA-256 of the file's bytes as the last read digest and the file's owner token and agent tokens as the current token list.",
     "load_installation: [RETURN_SHAPE] Returns the loaded Installation; a failed check propagates InstallationRejectedError and nothing is kept."
    ],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "The State 7 notes require read_configuration to check excessive depth after the file-read checks and before parsing, name that depth check in InstallationRejectedError, and require load_installation to propagate it.",
    "verified": true,
    "blocking": false
   }
  },
  {
   "topic": "json_depth result for malformed JSON input",
   "members": [
    "r1.00"
   ],
   "runs": [
    1
   ],
   "questions": [
    "What depth must json_depth return for malformed JSON bytes, including unterminated strings, invalid escapes, unmatched delimiters and invalid UTF-8?"
   ],
   "units": [
    "context"
   ]
  }
 ],
